import UnforcedLeray.Units.B0415.Cylindrical
import UnforcedLeray.Units.B0415.Commute

/-!
# Unit B0415 (`eq:free-stress-2`): the invariant (axisymmetric, no swirl) closed subspace of
`Y_q` and the equivariance of the free operators

Blueprint unit `B0415`, label `eq:free-stress-2`, `paper/main.tex` lines 7346–7362
(§`sec:st18-8879`, "Spaces, symmetry, and statement"):

> The optional symmetry restriction used here is the following exact closed subspace. Fields
> are axisymmetric under rotations about the third coordinate axis. If `J` is pushforward by
> reflection in a meridional plane, require `Jw(τ) = w(τ)` (eq:free-stress-2). In cylindrical
> components, `J` preserves the radial and axial components and reverses the azimuthal
> component, so these are the `𝒪`-invariant fields: axisymmetric without swirl. Tensors
> transform by pushforward in both indices; invariant tensors have no entry with exactly one
> azimuthal index. Rotation, reflection, and phase translation commute with spatial dilation,
> heat evolution, and Leray projection. Hence every assertion below restricts to this subspace.

## Formalization

* The phase space is `PhaseSpace.Yq P q = L^q(ℝ/Pℤ; L^q(ℝ³;ℂ³))` (decision D2 of

  isometry `g` of `ℝ³` acts by pushforward, slice by slice: `actY P q g`,
  `(g·w)(τ) = g w(τ)(g⁻¹·)` on real and imaginary parts (`B0415/Action.lean`). The rotation by
  `θ` about `e₃` is `Axi.rotZ θ`, and `J` is the pushforward by the reflection `σ = Axi.reflY`
  in the meridional plane `{y₁ = 0}` (`Lib/AxisymmetricB/Average.lean`).
* `Yaxi P q` (**the subspace of eq:free-stress-2**): `R_θ w = w` for every `θ` and `Jw = w`; a
  complex subspace, closed (`isClosed_Yaxi`).
* **(i)** `radial_J`, `axial_J`, `azimuthal_J` (cylindrical components; `B0415/Cylindrical`);
  `fixesAxis_cases` (`𝒪` is generated by the rotations and `σ`; `B0415/Group`);
  `Yaxi_eq_YO`: `Yaxi` is exactly the subspace `YO` of `𝒪`-invariant fields;
  `mem_Yaxi_iff_slices` (`q < ∞`): `w ∈ Yaxi` iff a.e. phase slice is axisymmetric without
  swirl in the sense of `Statement.IsAxisymmetricNoSwirl` (real and imaginary parts);
  `ae_noSwirl_of_mem_Yaxi`: the azimuthal components of a.e. slice vanish a.e.;
  `ae_eq_meridional`: an invariant measurable field is `A_r(ϱ, y₃) e_r + A_z(ϱ, y₃) e_z` a.e.
* **(ii)** `pushTensor` (pushforward in both indices), `pushTensor_outer`,
  `ae_isMeridTensor`: a measurable invariant tensor field has no frame entry with exactly one
  azimuthal index a.e. (`Axi.IsMeridTensor`).
* **(iii)** For every linear isometry `g` (so for `R_θ` and `J`) and every phase shift `σ`:
  `heatY_actY`, `dilY_actY`, `lerayY_actY`, `phaseY_heatY`, `phaseY_dilY`, `phaseY_lerayY`
  (`B0415/Commute`), with B0414's operators: `RieszLp.lerayY` (`1 < q < ∞`), the heat semigroup
  `Heat.heatLp` and the dilation `u ↦ u(b ·)` (`RieszLp.dilateLpE`, `q < ∞`) slice by slice, and
  `w ↦ w(σ + ·)`; also `phaseY_actY`.
* **(iv)** `mem_Yaxi_of_comm`: every map commuting with the rotations and `J` maps `Yaxi` into
  itself; `heatY_mem_Yaxi`, `dilY_mem_Yaxi`, `lerayY_mem_Yaxi`, `phaseY_mem_Yaxi`;
  `mem_Yaxi_of_fixedPoint`: the unique fixed point of a map commuting with the rotations and
  `J` lies in `Yaxi` (how fixed-point constructions restrict to the subspace).
* `Statement` bundles (i)–(iv); `statement : Statement`.

## Scope and conventions

* The subspace is defined for every `1 ≤ q ≤ ∞` and every period `P > 0`; the slice
  characterization (`mem_Yaxi_iff_slices`, `⇒`) uses `q < ∞` (continuity of the rotation
  orbit in `L^q`), which covers the manuscript's `1 < q < 3`.
* `IsAxisymmetricNoSwirl` (`lean/UnforcedLeray/Statement.lean`) is for real fields; a complex
  field is axisymmetric without swirl when its real and imaginary parts are (`IsAxiNoSwirlC`),
  which matches the componentwise action on complex fields.
* "Hence every assertion below restricts to this subspace" is formalized as the closedness of
  the subspace and its invariance under the operators named in the sentence (dilation, heat,
  Leray, phase translation) and under every map or fixed point commuting with `𝒪`. The
  equivariance of `νΔ`, `T₀` and of the distributional graph `D_(ν,q)` of B0411 under `𝒪` is not
  part of the sentence and is not stated here.

Junk values: no statement depends on a Lean convention. Everything is an `Lp` class or an a.e.
identity; on the axis Lean's `e_r = e_φ = 0`, the component identities hold at every point and
the a.e. statements discard the null axis; `Heat.heatLp _ _ θ` is the identity for `θ ≤ 0`, so
the heat commutation is trivially true there and the manuscript's claim for `θ > 0`.

Status: every asserted fact of the unit is proved, under the scope above. Theorem A is not
proved in Lean.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology

namespace UnforcedLeray.B0415

open UnforcedLeray.PhaseSpace (CVec3 Yq)
open UnforcedLeray.RieszLp (reV imV)
open UnforcedLeray.Axi (rotZ reflY eR eΦ e3 mer fixesAxis_rotZ fixesAxis_reflY)
open UnforcedLeray.Blueprint (rotateField)

variable {P : ℝ} [Fact (0 < P)] {q : ℝ≥0∞} [Fact (1 ≤ q)]

/-! ### The subspaces -/

variable (P q) in
/-- **The invariant subspace of eq:free-stress-2** (tex 7347–7352): fields of `Y_q` that are
axisymmetric under the rotations `R_θ` about the third axis and satisfy `Jw = w`, `J` the
pushforward by the reflection `σ` in the meridional plane `{y₁ = 0}`. -/
def Yaxi : Submodule ℂ (Yq P q) where
  carrier := {w | (∀ θ : ℝ, actY P q (rotZ θ) w = w) ∧ actY P q reflY w = w}
  add_mem' {v w} hv hw := by
    refine ⟨fun θ => ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [map_add, hv.1 θ, hw.1 θ]
    · rw [map_add, hv.2, hw.2]
  zero_mem' := ⟨fun θ => map_zero _, map_zero _⟩
  smul_mem' c w hw := by
    refine ⟨fun θ => ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [map_smul, hw.1 θ]
    · rw [map_smul, hw.2]

theorem mem_Yaxi (w : Yq P q) :
    w ∈ Yaxi P q ↔ (∀ θ : ℝ, actY P q (rotZ θ) w = w) ∧ actY P q reflY w = w := Iff.rfl

variable (P q) in
/-- The subspace of `𝒪`-invariant fields: `g·w = w` for every linear isometry `g` fixing `e₃`
(tex 112–115, 7355–7356). -/
def YO : Submodule ℂ (Yq P q) where
  carrier := {w | ∀ g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space, FixesAxis g → actY P q g w = w}
  add_mem' {v w} hv hw g hg := by rw [map_add, hv g hg, hw g hg]
  zero_mem' g _ := map_zero _
  smul_mem' c w hw g hg := by rw [map_smul, hw g hg]

theorem mem_YO (w : Yq P q) :
    w ∈ YO P q ↔ ∀ g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space, FixesAxis g → actY P q g w = w := Iff.rfl

/-- **The subspace is closed** (tex 7346: "exact closed subspace"). -/
theorem isClosed_Yaxi : IsClosed (Yaxi P q : Set (Yq P q)) := by
  have h : (Yaxi P q : Set (Yq P q)) =
      (⋂ θ : ℝ, {w : Yq P q | actY P q (rotZ θ) w = w}) ∩ {w | actY P q reflY w = w} := by
    ext w
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, mem_Yaxi, mem_inter_iff, mem_iInter, mem_ofPred_eq]
  rw [h]
  exact (isClosed_iInter fun θ => isClosed_eq (actY P q (rotZ θ)).continuous continuous_id).inter
    (isClosed_eq (actY P q reflY).continuous continuous_id)

/-! ### (i) The subspace is exactly the `𝒪`-invariant fields -/

/-- **(i)** The fields satisfying eq:free-stress-2 are exactly the `𝒪`-invariant fields
(tex 7355–7356): `𝒪` is generated by the rotations about `e₃` and the reflection `σ`. -/
theorem Yaxi_eq_YO : Yaxi P q = YO P q := by
  ext w
  rw [mem_Yaxi, mem_YO]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hrot, hJ⟩ g hg
    obtain ⟨θ, rfl | rfl⟩ := fixesAxis_cases hg
    · exact hrot θ
    · rw [actY_trans, hJ, hrot θ]
  · intro h
    exact ⟨fun θ => h _ (fixesAxis_rotZ θ), h _ fixesAxis_reflY⟩

/-- **(i), slice form** (tex 7347–7356): for `q < ∞`, `w ∈ Y_q` satisfies eq:free-stress-2 iff
for a.e. phase `τ` the slice `w(τ)` is axisymmetric without swirl (`IsAxiNoSwirlC`: real and
imaginary parts satisfy `Statement.IsAxisymmetricNoSwirl`). The implication `⇐` holds for every
`q`. -/
theorem mem_Yaxi_iff_slices (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (w : Yq P q) :
    w ∈ Yaxi P q ↔
      ∀ᵐ τ ∂AddCircle.haarAddCircle, IsAxiNoSwirlC ((w τ : Lp CVec3 q volume) : Space → CVec3) := by
  constructor
  · intro hw
    rw [mem_Yaxi] at hw
    have hrat : ∀ᵐ τ ∂AddCircle.haarAddCircle (T := P),
        ∀ r : ℚ, actLp q (rotZ r) (w τ) = w τ :=
      ae_all_iff.2 fun r => (actY_eq_self_iff _ w).1 (hw.1 r)
    filter_upwards [hrat, (actY_eq_self_iff _ w).1 hw.2] with τ h1 h2
    exact (isAxiNoSwirlC_iff_actLp (w τ)).2 fun g hg => actLp_of_generators hq h1 h2 hg
  · intro hw
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, (show (Yaxi P q : Set (Yq P q)) = YO P q by rw [Yaxi_eq_YO])]
    intro g hg
    refine (actY_eq_self_iff g w).2 ?_
    filter_upwards [hw] with τ hτ
    exact (isAxiNoSwirlC_iff_actLp (w τ)).1 hτ g hg

/-- **(i), no swirl on the slices**: for `w` in the subspace (`q < ∞`), for a.e. phase `τ` the
azimuthal components of the real and imaginary parts of `w(τ)` vanish a.e. -/
theorem ae_noSwirl_of_mem_Yaxi (hq : q ≠ ⊤) {w : Yq P q} (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) :
    ∀ᵐ τ ∂AddCircle.haarAddCircle, (∀ᵐ y, inner ℝ (reV ((w τ : Lp CVec3 q volume) y)) (eΦ y) = 0) ∧
      (∀ᵐ y, inner ℝ (imV ((w τ : Lp CVec3 q volume) y)) (eΦ y) = 0) := by
  filter_upwards [(mem_Yaxi_iff_slices hq w).1 hw] with τ hτ
  have hm : Measurable ((w τ : Lp CVec3 q volume) : Space → CVec3) :=
    (Lp.stronglyMeasurable (w τ)).measurable
  exact ⟨ae_azimuthal_eq_zero (reV.continuous.measurable.comp hm) hτ.1,
    ae_azimuthal_eq_zero (imV.continuous.measurable.comp hm) hτ.2⟩

/-! ### (iv) Restriction to the subspace -/

/-- **(iv)** A map commuting with the rotations `R_θ` and with `J` maps the subspace into
itself. -/
theorem mem_Yaxi_of_comm (T : Yq P q → Yq P q)
    (hrot : ∀ θ : ℝ, ∀ v, T (actY P q (rotZ θ) v) = actY P q (rotZ θ) (T v))
    (hJ : ∀ v, T (actY P q reflY v) = actY P q reflY (T v)) {w : Yq P q}
    (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) : T w ∈ Yaxi P q := by
  refine ⟨fun θ => ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← hrot, hw.1 θ]
  · rw [← hJ, hw.2]

/-- **(iv), fixed points.** If `T` commutes with the rotations and `J` and has at most one fixed
point, its fixed point lies in the subspace. -/
theorem mem_Yaxi_of_fixedPoint (T : Yq P q → Yq P q)
    (hrot : ∀ θ : ℝ, ∀ v, T (actY P q (rotZ θ) v) = actY P q (rotZ θ) (T v))
    (hJ : ∀ v, T (actY P q reflY v) = actY P q reflY (T v))
    (huniq : ∀ v v', T v = v → T v' = v' → v = v') {w : Yq P q} (hw : T w = w) :
    w ∈ Yaxi P q := by
  refine ⟨fun θ => huniq _ _ ?_ hw, huniq _ _ ?_ hw⟩
  · rw [hrot, hw]
  · rw [hJ, hw]

/-- **(iv)** The heat evolution preserves the subspace. -/
theorem heatY_mem_Yaxi (θ : ℝ) {w : Yq P q} (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) : heatY P q θ w ∈ Yaxi P q :=
  mem_Yaxi_of_comm (heatY P q θ) (fun _ v => heatY_actY _ θ v) (fun v => heatY_actY _ θ v) hw

/-- **(iv)** The spatial dilation preserves the subspace (`q < ∞`, `b ≠ 0`). -/
theorem dilY_mem_Yaxi (hq : q ≠ ⊤) {b : ℝ} (hb : b ≠ 0) {w : Yq P q} (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) :
    dilY P hq hb w ∈ Yaxi P q :=
  mem_Yaxi_of_comm (dilY P hq hb) (fun _ v => dilY_actY hq hb _ v) (fun v => dilY_actY hq hb _ v)
    hw

/-- **(iv)** The Leray projection preserves the subspace (`1 < q < ∞`). -/
theorem lerayY_mem_Yaxi (hq1 : 1 < q) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) {w : Yq P q} (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) :
    RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq w ∈ Yaxi P q :=
  mem_Yaxi_of_comm (RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq) (fun _ v => lerayY_actY hq1 hq _ v)
    (fun v => lerayY_actY hq1 hq _ v) hw

/-- **(iv)** Phase translation preserves the subspace. -/
theorem phaseY_mem_Yaxi (σ : AddCircle P) {w : Yq P q} (hw : w ∈ Yaxi P q) :
    phaseY σ w ∈ Yaxi P q :=
  mem_Yaxi_of_comm (phaseY σ) (fun _ v => phaseY_actY σ _ v) (fun v => phaseY_actY σ _ v) hw

/-! ### The unit -/

/-- **B0415 (i)** (tex 7353–7356): in cylindrical components `J` preserves the radial and axial
components and reverses the azimuthal one; `𝒪` is generated by the rotations about `e₃` and the
meridional reflection; the subspace of eq:free-stress-2 is exactly the `𝒪`-invariant subspace,
and (for `q < ∞`) exactly the fields whose a.e. phase slice is axisymmetric without swirl; an
invariant measurable field has no swirl and is meridional a.e. -/
def Statement_i : Prop :=
  (∀ (f : Space → Space) (y : Space),
      inner ℝ (rotateField reflY f y) (eR y) = inner ℝ (f (reflY y)) (eR (reflY y)) ∧
      rotateField reflY f y 2 = f (reflY y) 2 ∧
      inner ℝ (rotateField reflY f y) (eΦ y) = -inner ℝ (f (reflY y)) (eΦ (reflY y))) ∧
    (∀ g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space, FixesAxis g → ∃ θ : ℝ, g = rotZ θ ∨ g = reflY.trans (rotZ θ)) ∧
    (∀ (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)], Yaxi P q = YO P q) ∧
    (∀ (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)], q ≠ ⊤ → ∀ w : Yq P q,
      w ∈ Yaxi P q ↔ ∀ᵐ τ ∂AddCircle.haarAddCircle,
        IsAxiNoSwirlC ((w τ : Lp CVec3 q volume) : Space → CVec3)) ∧
    (∀ f : Space → Space, Measurable f → IsAxisymmetricNoSwirl f →
      (∀ᵐ y, inner ℝ (f y) (eΦ y) = 0) ∧
      ∃ Ar Az : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ, Measurable Ar ∧ Measurable Az ∧
        f =ᵐ[volume] fun y => Ar (mer y) • eR y + Az (mer y) • e3)

theorem statement_i : Statement_i :=
  ⟨fun f y => ⟨radial_J f y, axial_J f y, azimuthal_J f y⟩, fun _ hg => fixesAxis_cases hg,
    fun _ _ _ _ => Yaxi_eq_YO, fun _ _ _ _ hq w => mem_Yaxi_iff_slices hq w,
    fun _ hf hsym => ⟨ae_azimuthal_eq_zero hf hsym, ae_eq_meridional hf hsym⟩⟩

/-- **B0415 (ii)** (tex 7356–7357): tensors transform by pushforward in both indices (so
`u ⊗ v ↦ (g·u) ⊗ (g·v)`); a measurable invariant tensor field has no frame entry with exactly
one azimuthal index, a.e. -/
def Statement_ii : Prop :=
  (∀ (g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space) (u v : Space → Space),
      pushTensor g (fun x => outer (u x) (v x)) =
        fun x => outer (rotateField g u x) (rotateField g v x)) ∧
    ∀ T : Space → Space →L[ℝ] Space, Measurable T → IsInvariantTensor T →
      ∀ᵐ y, Axi.IsMeridTensor (frameEntries T y)

theorem statement_ii : Statement_ii :=
  ⟨pushTensor_outer, fun _ hT hinv => ae_isMeridTensor hT hinv⟩

/-- **B0415 (iii)** (tex 7358–7360): rotation and reflection (every linear isometry `g` of
`ℝ³`) and phase translation commute with spatial dilation, heat evolution and Leray projection
on `Y_q`. -/
def Statement_iii (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)] : Prop :=
  (∀ (g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space) (θ : ℝ) (w : Yq P q),
      heatY P q θ (actY P q g w) = actY P q g (heatY P q θ w)) ∧
    (∀ (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (b : ℝ) (hb : b ≠ 0) (g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space) (w : Yq P q),
      dilY P hq hb (actY P q g w) = actY P q g (dilY P hq hb w)) ∧
    (∀ (hq1 : 1 < q) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space) (w : Yq P q),
      RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq (actY P q g w) = actY P q g (RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq w)) ∧
    (∀ (σ : AddCircle P) (θ : ℝ) (w : Yq P q),
      phaseY σ (heatY P q θ w) = heatY P q θ (phaseY σ w)) ∧
    (∀ (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (b : ℝ) (hb : b ≠ 0) (σ : AddCircle P) (w : Yq P q),
      phaseY σ (dilY P hq hb w) = dilY P hq hb (phaseY σ w)) ∧
    (∀ (hq1 : 1 < q) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (σ : AddCircle P) (w : Yq P q),
      phaseY σ (RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq w) = RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq (phaseY σ w)) ∧
    (∀ (σ : AddCircle P) (g : Space ≃ₗᵢ[ℝ] Space) (w : Yq P q),
      phaseY σ (actY P q g w) = actY P q g (phaseY σ w))

theorem statement_iii (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)] : Statement_iii P q :=
  ⟨heatY_actY, fun hq _ hb => dilY_actY hq hb, lerayY_actY, phaseY_heatY,
    fun hq _ hb => phaseY_dilY hq hb, phaseY_lerayY, phaseY_actY⟩

/-- **B0415 (iv)** (tex 7346, 7360–7361): the subspace is closed, and every assertion restricts
to it: it is preserved by heat evolution, dilation, Leray projection and phase translation, by
every map commuting with the rotations and `J`, and it contains the unique fixed point of such
a map. -/
def Statement_iv (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)] : Prop :=
  IsClosed (Yaxi P q : Set (Yq P q)) ∧
    (∀ (θ : ℝ) (w : Yq P q), w ∈ Yaxi P q → heatY P q θ w ∈ Yaxi P q) ∧
    (∀ (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (b : ℝ) (hb : b ≠ 0) (w : Yq P q), w ∈ Yaxi P q →
      dilY P hq hb w ∈ Yaxi P q) ∧
    (∀ (hq1 : 1 < q) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) (w : Yq P q), w ∈ Yaxi P q →
      RieszLp.lerayY P q hq1 hq w ∈ Yaxi P q) ∧
    (∀ (σ : AddCircle P) (w : Yq P q), w ∈ Yaxi P q → phaseY σ w ∈ Yaxi P q) ∧
    (∀ T : Yq P q → Yq P q,
      (∀ θ : ℝ, ∀ v, T (actY P q (rotZ θ) v) = actY P q (rotZ θ) (T v)) →
      (∀ v, T (actY P q reflY v) = actY P q reflY (T v)) →
      (∀ w, w ∈ Yaxi P q → T w ∈ Yaxi P q) ∧
      ((∀ v v', T v = v → T v' = v' → v = v') → ∀ w, T w = w → w ∈ Yaxi P q))

theorem statement_iv (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)] : Statement_iv P q :=
  ⟨isClosed_Yaxi, fun θ _ hw => heatY_mem_Yaxi θ hw, fun hq _ hb _ hw => dilY_mem_Yaxi hq hb hw,
    fun hq1 hq _ hw => lerayY_mem_Yaxi hq1 hq hw, fun σ _ hw => phaseY_mem_Yaxi σ hw,
    fun T hrot hJ => ⟨fun _ hw => mem_Yaxi_of_comm T hrot hJ hw,
      fun huniq _ hw => mem_Yaxi_of_fixedPoint T hrot hJ huniq hw⟩⟩

/-- **B0415** (`eq:free-stress-2`, `paper/main.tex` lines 7346–7362): the invariant
(axisymmetric, no swirl) closed subspace `Yaxi P q` of `Y_q` and the equivariance of the
spatial operators, claims (i)–(iv). -/
def Statement : Prop :=
  Statement_i ∧ Statement_ii ∧
    (∀ (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)], Statement_iii P q) ∧
    (∀ (P : ℝ) [Fact (0 < P)] (q : ℝ≥0∞) [Fact (1 ≤ q)], Statement_iv P q)

/-- **B0415**, proved (see the module docstring for the scope). -/
theorem statement : Statement :=
  ⟨statement_i, statement_ii, fun P _ q _ => statement_iii P q, fun P _ q _ => statement_iv P q⟩

end UnforcedLeray.B0415
